# Your keyboard shortcuts.
#
# lumen reads this file before its own (~/.config/sxhkd/sxhkdrc), so a key
# here replaces lumen's. It's yours: lumen updates never change it. Apply
# changes with super + Escape. They show in super + / under "Your shortcuts".
#
# The keys on one line, the command on the next, indented with a tab. A
# comment right above the keys is their description in super + /.
# Key names: super, shift, ctrl, alt, Return, space, Tab, Escape, Print,
# a-z, 0-9, F1-F12, Left/Right/Up/Down... (run `xev` to see a key's name).
#
# Remove the "#" in front of the lines to use an example.

# # Firefox
# super + b
# 	firefox

# # Calculator
# super + shift + c
# 	gnome-calculator

# # A different terminal (replaces lumen's super + Return)
# super + Return
# 	alacritty

# # Screenshot of the whole screen, clipboard only (replaces lumen's ctrl + Print)
# ctrl + Print
# 	lumen-capture shot screen --copy

# # Volume up and down on super + F3 / F2
# super + {F2,F3}
# 	wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 5%{-,+}
